Info: 
Usage: openETPServer [global-options] server --start -d conn_string [options]

Actions:
  -h [ --help ]                         Display this information
  --init                                Initialize main DB
  --check                               Check main DB
  --start                               Start ETP 1.2 server

Options:
  -P [ --port ] arg (=9002)             Specify port to listen to
  --reuseAddressSocket arg (=1)         Reuse socket address. Allows reusing 
                                        socket port
                                        shortly after previous server instance 
                                        stopped.
  --stopOnLastDisconnection arg (=1)    Stop when last client disconnect
  --ipv4 arg (=0)                       Use ipv4 protocol instead of ipv6
  --maxConnections arg (=-1)            Specify maximum number of connections
  -d [ --db-connection ] arg            PostgreSQL connection string (If not 
                                        defined, will use POSTGRESQL_CONN_STRIN
                                        G environment variable
  -s [ --space-path ] arg               ETP dataspace name (folder or 
                                        folder/project)
  --space-guid arg                      ETP dataspace guid (uses path if 
                                        omitted)
  --xdata-file arg                      New Space meta-data as JSON file (on 
                                        EPC Direct-import)
  --xdata arg                           New Space meta-data as JSON (on EPC 
                                        Direct-import)
  --vacuum                              Vacuum (i.e. optimize) DB, post EPC 
                                        Direct-import
  --no-default-space                    Omit ETP 1.2 mandatory 'default' 
                                        dataspace on --init
  --overwrite                           Overwrite existing EPC on Direct-import
  --check-activities arg (=1)           Check if new data has corresponding 
                                        activity
  --auth arg                            Deprecated: Legacy name of authN
  -N [ --authN ] arg (=builtin)         Authentication: 'none', 'builtin', or 
                                        'delegate=URL'
  --authZ arg (=none)                   Authorization:  'none', 'builtin',
                                        'delegate=URL', or 'policyDelegate=URL'
  -k [ --jwt-secret ] arg               JWT Signing Key (--authN=builtin only).
  -j [ --jobs ] [=arg(=0)]              How many worker-threads:
                                        * not specified: Defaults to 
                                        single-threaded;
                                        * -j: Use as many threads as hardware 
                                        cores;
                                        * -jN: Use exactly N threads
  --force                               Continue instead of exit, on some 
                                        warnings/errors

Connect Options:
  -S [ --server-url ] arg               ETP 1.2 server URL
  --etp-trace arg                       Trace ETP messages to file
                                        Filename inferred if empty or directory
  --timeout arg (=10s,10s)              ETP timeouts for CONNECT and GET/PUT 
                                        requests
  -M [ --max-msg-size ] arg (=16MB, 128MB)
                                        Maximum WebSocket message size(s) in 
                                        bytes
  -B [ --max-batch-size ] arg (=1000000)
                                        Maximum parts per multi-part message
  -Q [ --msg-queue-depth ] arg (=500)   Deprecated: Maximum concurrent 
                                        (in-flight) messages
  --acknowledge                         Set Acknowledge flag on all ETP 
                                        requests
  -Z [ --compress ] arg (=gzip)         Set Compress-Body flag on all ETP 
                                        requests
                                        Specify compressor(s) (Default: gzip)
  --shun-protocols arg                  Force client to ignore those protocols

Info: openETPServer: done.
